> vector ``. Chasing through traceback,  db_query_fields(object$src$con,
> object$from) in tbl-sql.r#55 returns NULL and this happens because the
> default db_query-field.DBIConnection appends a ``WHERE 0=1`` to the select
> clause. Why is this condition appended in the default method?

It puts WHERE 0=1 to ensure that the database do any computation.  You
might need to override db_query_fields. For example, src_sqlite has:

#' @export
db_query_fields.SQLiteConnection <- function(con, sql, ...) {
  rs <- dbSendQuery(con, paste0("SELECT * FROM ", sql))
  on.exit(dbClearResult(rs))

  names(fetch(rs, 0L))
}

Hadley

